    "lessonPlan": "time: 0-5 minutes\nsegment: Start questions\ntask: Answer the three start questions honestly and briefly.\n\ntime: 5-12 minutes\nsegment: Teach\ntask: Read or listen to the lesson transcript and identify the main parenting skill.\n\ntime: 12-22 minutes\nsegment: Activity 1\ntask: Complete Notice the Pattern.\n\ntime: 22-34 minutes\nsegment: Activity 2\ntask: Complete Practise the Safer Response.\n\ntime: 34-37 minutes\nsegment: Quiz\ntask: Complete the quick knowledge check.\n\ntime: 37-40 minutes\nsegment: Reflection and evidence\ntask: Answer the reflection questions and choose one evidence item to save or upload.",
    "practiceActivities": "name: Activity 1: Notice the Pattern\ndurationMinutes: 10\ninstructions: Write one recent or realistic example connected to Core emotions. Record the trigger, the child’s likely feeling or need, the adult response, and one safer response to practise next time.\nevidencePrompt: Save the completed pattern note as a reflection or learning record.\n\nname: Activity 2: Practise the Safer Response\ndurationMinutes: 12\ninstructions: Create one sentence, routine, limit, repair statement or practical action that applies Core emotions in daily life. Keep it short enough to use when stressed.\nevidencePrompt: Upload the sentence, plan, checklist, script or routine change you created.",
    "knowledgeCheck": "question: A dysregulated child usually learns better after their body has calmed.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Calming the nervous system improves listening, thinking and repair.\n\nquestion: The main aim of Core emotions is to practise one safer response, not to become perfect in one session.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: SAFE STEPS lessons focus on practical progress, reflection and repeated safe action.\n\nquestion: Evidence of change can include reflection notes, routines, plans, repair statements, checklists or examples of safer communication.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Evidence can show effort, insight, follow-through and changed behaviour over time.",
    "evidenceTask": "Upload or write one short evidence item showing how you practised Core emotions. This may be a reflection, routine plan, safety action, communication script, checklist, repair statement or daily-life example.",
    "reflectionQuestions": "What did I learn about Core emotions?\n\nWhat is one thing I need to stop, start or keep doing?\n\nHow could this help my child feel safer, calmer or more supported?\n\nWhat will I practise this week?",
    "afterQuestion": "After this lesson, what does Core emotions mean to me now?"
