    "practiceActivities": "name: Activity 1: Notice the Pattern\ndurationMinutes: 10\ninstructions: Write one recent or realistic example connected to Digital wellbeing. Record the trigger, the child’s likely feeling or need, the adult response, and one safer response to practise next time.\nevidencePrompt: Save the completed pattern note as a reflection or learning record.\n\nname: Activity 2: Practise the Safer Response\ndurationMinutes: 12\ninstructions: Create one sentence, routine, limit, repair statement or practical action that applies Digital wellbeing in daily life. Keep it short enough to use when stressed.\nevidencePrompt: Upload the sentence, plan, checklist, script or routine change you created.",
    "knowledgeCheck": "question: One small repeated skill can show meaningful change over time.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Change is usually shown through repeated safe actions, not one perfect moment.\n\nquestion: The main aim of Digital wellbeing is to practise one safer response, not to become perfect in one session.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: SAFE STEPS lessons focus on practical progress, reflection and repeated safe action.\n\nquestion: Evidence of change can include reflection notes, routines, plans, repair statements, checklists or examples of safer communication.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Evidence can show effort, insight, follow-through and changed behaviour over time.",
    "evidenceTask": "Upload or write one short evidence item showing how you practised Digital wellbeing. This may be a reflection, routine plan, safety action, communication script, checklist, repair statement or daily-life example.",
    "reflectionQuestions": "What did I learn about Digital wellbeing?\n\nWhat is one thing I need to stop, start or keep doing?\n\nHow could this help my child feel safer, calmer or more supported?\n\nWhat will I practise this week?",
    "afterQuestion": "After this lesson, what does Digital wellbeing mean to me now?"
