    "knowledgeCheck": "question: A dysregulated child usually learns better after their body has calmed.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Calming the nervous system improves listening, thinking and repair.\n\nquestion: The main aim of Emotional Regulation for Parents is to practise one safer response, not to become perfect in one session.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: SAFE STEPS lessons focus on practical progress, reflection and repeated safe action.\n\nquestion: Evidence of change can include reflection notes, routines, plans, repair statements, checklists or examples of safer communication.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Evidence can show effort, insight, follow-through and changed behaviour over time.",
