    "practiceActivities": "name: Activity 1: Notice the Pattern\ndurationMinutes: 10\ninstructions: Write one recent or realistic example connected to Logical Consequences - Accountability. Record the trigger, the child’s likely feeling or need, the adult response, and one safer response to practise next time.\nevidencePrompt: Save the completed pattern note as a reflection or learning record.\n\nname: Activity 2: Practise the Safer Response\ndurationMinutes: 12\ninstructions: Create one sentence, routine, limit, repair statement or practical action that applies Logical Consequences - Accountability in daily life. Keep it short enough to use when stressed.\nevidencePrompt: Upload the sentence, plan, checklist, script or routine change you created.",
    "knowledgeCheck": "question: Discipline is most effective when it teaches a safer replacement skill.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Safe discipline combines connection, clear limits, teaching and follow-through.\n\nquestion: The main aim of Logical Consequences - Accountability is to practise one safer response, not to become perfect in one session.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: SAFE STEPS lessons focus on practical progress, reflection and repeated safe action.\n\nquestion: Evidence of change can include reflection notes, routines, plans, repair statements, checklists or examples of safer communication.\noptions: True\n\nFalse\nanswer: True\nexplanation: Evidence can show effort, insight, follow-through and changed behaviour over time.",
