    "teachingTranscript": "Lesson title: Reducing Chaos in the Home - Regulation Safety\n\nQuick question before this lesson: Before this lesson starts, what does Reducing Chaos in the Home - Regulation Safety mean to me?\n\nThis lesson turns Reducing Chaos in the Home - Regulation Safety into a practical parenting skill that can be noticed, practised and recorded in daily life.\n\nFor trauma-affected children, behaviour can be a nervous-system response rather than deliberate defiance. The parent’s job is to lower threat, create safety and then teach skills when the child is calm enough to learn.\n\nStart by thinking about where Reducing Chaos in the Home - Regulation Safety shows up in your home. It may appear during routines, discipline, communication, health care, school mornings, contact visits, co-parenting exchanges, or moments when a child has big feelings. The key is to slow down enough to notice the pattern before reacting.\n\nA safe parenting response usually has four parts: pause, check the child’s need, choose a calm response, and follow through consistently. This does not mean letting children do whatever they want. It means guiding behaviour without fear, shame or confusion.\n\nFor this topic, choose one real example from your family life. Write down what happened, what the child may have needed, what you did, and what you could try next time. This creates evidence of insight and change because it shows thinking, planning and follow-through.\n\nFinish the lesson by choosing one action you can practise during the next week. Keep it small enough to repeat. A small action done consistently is stronger evidence than a large plan that is not used.",
    "lessonPlan": "time: 0-5 minutes\nsegment: Opening title and quick question\ntask: Display the lesson title. Answer the quick question before reading the lesson.\n\ntime: 5-12 minutes\nsegment: Teach\ntask: Read or listen to the lesson transcript and identify the main parenting skill.\n\ntime: 12-22 minutes\nsegment: Activity 1\ntask: Complete Notice the Pattern.\n\ntime: 22-34 minutes\nsegment: Activity 2\ntask: Complete Practise the Safer Response.\n\ntime: 34-37 minutes\nsegment: Quiz\ntask: Complete the quick knowledge check.\n\ntime: 37-40 minutes\nsegment: Reflection and evidence\ntask: Answer the reflection questions and choose one evidence item to save or upload.",
